https://github.com/tessera-io/platform/pull/389

Retries are now exponential with full jitter: base 2s, cap 5 minutes, max 8 attempts, then the feed goes to "degraded" instead of silently dying. Per the design doc, minus the circuit breaker, which is a follow-up.

Please read the state machine in connector/retry.py first; the rest is plumbing. Tests include a flapping-feed simulation that I am slightly too proud of.

